BOUNDARY DATA — SOURCES AND ATTRIBUTION
=======================================

The .geojson files in this folder are third-party boundary data. Every value below is taken
VERBATIM from the upstream metadata (the geoBoundaries API, https://www.geoboundaries.org/api/current/gbOpen/<ISO3>/<LEVEL>/).
Nothing here is our own wording about a licence.

gb-IND-ADM1-full.geojson, gb-IND-ADM1-full-web.geojson
  source          geoBoundaries gbOpen (www.geoboundaries.org)
  boundaryID      IND-ADM1-1811400
  licence         Creative Commons Attribution 2.5 India (CC BY 2.5 IN)
  licenceSource   github.com/datameet/maps
  year            2011
  ATTRIBUTION IS REQUIRED for this file: it is Creative Commons Attribution, so a work that
  redistributes or displays it must credit the source above.

gb-IND-ADM1.geojson, gb-IND-ADM1-web.geojson
  The same India ADM1 boundary as above, curated to the UPG-100 list's partition.
  Same source, same boundaryID, same licence, same attribution duty.

gb-CHN-ADM1.geojson
  source          geoBoundaries gbOpen (www.geoboundaries.org)
  boundaryID      CHN-ADM1-43563684
  licence         Public Domain
  licenceSource   commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File
  year            2019
  No attribution duty: upstream records this boundary as Public Domain.

world-adm0.geojson, world-adm0-web.geojson
  source          geoBoundaries gbOpen (www.geoboundaries.org), assembled per country
  features        162 countries
  licence         MIXED — and now ESTABLISHED per country, not merely acknowledged.
  THE PER-COUNTRY TABLE IS THE AUTHORITY, and it lives in ONE place on purpose:
      plugin-designs/my-upg-100-list/data/adm0/PROVENANCE.json
  It records boundaryLicense, licenseSource and boundaryID for all 162, each value taken
  verbatim from https://www.geoboundaries.org/api/current/gbOpen/<ISO3>/<LEVEL>/ (162 queries,
  0 failures, one spot-check re-verified against the live API). This file deliberately does NOT
  copy that table: one table in two places drifts.

  130 OF THE 162 CARRY A DUTY. Only 32 are duty-free (28 Public Domain, 4 CC0). By class:

    ATTRIBUTION-ONLY (credit the source)
      44  CC BY 4.0        13  CC BY 3.0 IGO        4  CC BY 2.5        2  CC BY 3.0
      2  Open Government Licence v3

    SHARE-ALIKE CLASS — A STRONGER DUTY: a derivative may have to be licensed alike, which is
    the class that actually constrains giving this repository away.
      58  Open Data Commons ODbL 1.0
       7  Creative Commons ShareAlike 2.0 / 3.0 — AGO GAB GEO GIN MMR NER TUR

    ODbL IS LISTED IN THAT CLASS DELIBERATELY. Alongside attribution it requires a Derivative
    Database to be offered under ODbL and carries a keep-open provision, so by volume the
    share-alike question covers 65 of 162 countries, not 7. This repository has already acted on
    that reading once: library/scripts/posters/data/README.md records that Natural Earth's 1:10m
    ROADS were requested and deliberately NOT shipped because of an ODbL obligation.
    WHETHER 'licensed alike' binds a giveaway of this repository is a legal question, not a
    measurement, and it is open. It is recorded here so nobody has to rediscover it.

    duty-free: 28 Public Domain, 4 CC0.

See documentation/THIRD-PARTY.md for the whole shipped tree.
